SUMMARY:Rattlesnake Lodge to Folk Art Center along the MST  10 miles\, 140
 0' elevation
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Meeting Spot**: Folk Art Center 
 on the Blue Ridge Parkway. Prompt 8:00 departure\n**Description**: This is
  a point to point hike. We will meet at the Folk Art Center and shuttle up
  to the Rattle Snake Lodge starting point. Follow the MST Trail from the r
 emnants of the Rattlesnake Lodge\, a turn of the century lodge built by an
  Asheville physician\, to the Folk Art Center. There is a large variety of
  colorful wildflowers along the trail\, which is mostly downhill with a fe
 w short climbs. There is a nice overlook for a lunch/snack break. Good foo
 ting. Shaded. Pace: 2.4 mph. Dogs welcome if on a leash. **Please Note:** 
 This is a longer hike than my usual. If it's a warm day\, I recommend brin
 ging along extra water.\n\n**Courtesy\, (Please Abide!)**\n\n**Only sign u
 p if you \\*truly\\* plan to come.** If you must cancel\, please change yo
 ur status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24
  hours of the hike so wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please 
 please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Gro
 up event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the m
 eetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm t
 hat they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\,
  and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither y
 our hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor e
 liminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuri
 es\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316914824
 /
