SUMMARY:Rice Pinnacle Lollipop: 5.3 mi.\, 530 ft. Elev. Gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens 8:00 PM\, Sunday 
 October 11th]**\n\n**Please read the carpool info below the hike descripti
 on.**\n\nThis is a typical lovely hike in the Bent Creek area. It incorpor
 ates segments from the Wolf Branch and Corvair Trails\, along with several
  connectors. At 5.3 miles and a tame 530' elevation gain\, I'd rate it 2.5
  on a 0-10 difficulty scale. We'll average around 2.4 mph -- not a fitness
  hike\, but you should have enough experience hiking to know you can deal 
 with mild hills and a moderate pace.\n\nWe'll stop for a brief snack & wat
 er break halfway around. Wear sensible hiking boots. If you're on the fenc
 e about hiking poles\, you probably don't need them for this one.\n\n***Do
 g Policy:*** Dogs are extremely welcome but must be leashed.\n\n***Guest P
 olicy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they should join the Asheville 
 Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Alternatively\, contac
 t me in advance and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1" after you've made it 
 onto the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, I MAY be able to a
 dd your guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME AND PLACE**\nOptional carpooling on this 
 hike\, but it's encouraged. We'll rendezvous at the **Asheville Outlets pa
 rking lot\, just behind the Waffle House on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191)**. We'll
  leave there and head over to the Rice Pinnacle parking lot at **8:45 am**
 .\n\nIf you're parking at the trailhead\, please come a few minutes early 
 for check-in and intros. Look for me at my silver Hyundai. We'll hit the t
 rail a.s.a.p. after 9:00 AM.\n\n**DIRECTIONS TO TRAILHEAD**\n\n* From Exit
  33 on I-26\,\n* Head south on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191) for 2 miles\n* Right 
 at the lights on Bent Creek Ranch Rd.\n* After .3 miles bear left onto Wes
 ley Branch Rd.\n* Go about 1.4 miles and turn right just past the sign for
  the Rice Pinnacle Trailhead\n* Go left at the fork. You'll see the parkin
 g lot after a short distance.\n\n**Click here for the location on [Google 
 Maps](https://maps.app.goo.gl/totfTN3YMWYcU9KE7)**\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-L
 ISTERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly sign up if you \\*TRULY\\* plan to come. If
  you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as pos
 sible so wait-listers will have sufficient notice. And please please PLEAS
 E don't be a no-show.\n\nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep checking the
  evening before. Despite what I wrote above\, we always get last-minute dr
 opouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll monitor National Weather Service forecasts fo
 r the hike area and email cancellation messages by 7:30 AM if the forecast
  is for more than a 50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you
  have any questions\, message me through MeetUp until 8:30 AM the day of. 
 Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text or call me up to t
 he start of the hike: (803) 767-3094.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**LEGALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group
  event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the mee
 tup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and\, by joini
 ng a hike\, affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical condit
 ioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and
  property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can elim
 inate all risks or be responsible for your well-being. Participants assume
  full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
