SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Camino Primitivo - with WNC American Pilgrims
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of American Pil
 grims on the Camino. The route has been announced on the [Facebook Group P
 age](https://www.facebook.com/groups/AVLCamino/announcements).\nIf you are
  unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n[Americ
 an Pilgrims on the Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/w
 estern-north-carolina/)\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Way_(2010_film
 )](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Way_(2010_film))\nThis route is inspi
 red by the Camino Primitivo\, which has more hills than most of the other 
 routes to Santiago de Compostela.\n\n**Start:** 9:00 AM. Please arrive 10 
 minutes early.\n**Meeting Place:** Ingles\, 915 Merrimon Ave at the corner
  of Beaverdam Rd\; meet in the corner of the parking lot near the Ingles s
 ign and near Beaverdam Rd. Restrooms are available.\n**Full Distance:** 10
 .7 miles\n**Shorter Options:** 6\, 7\, or 8 miles\n**Elevation Gain:** 156
 0 feet\n**Duration:** Allow 6 hours with lunch stop\n**Hike Leader:** Maur
 ice Frank\n**Overview:**\nThis challenging high elevation gain walk is ins
 pired by the Camino Primitivo. We begin and end at Ingles on Merrimon Aven
 ue and Beaverdam Rd.\nOur first stage is a warm up on rolling hills throug
 h the beautiful heavily wooded Sherwood Heights neighborhood. Crossing ove
 r via Windsor Rd we reach the Reynolds Mountain community. We stop to rest
 \, hydrate and have a snack.\nIn the next section we steeply ascend up and
  around the top with beautiful long-range views. After lunch at The Villag
 e Porch in Reynolds Mountain we return around the back of Beaver Lake.\nTh
 ere are several options for a shorter less strenuous walk of about 6\, 7\,
  or 8 miles. The Sherwood Heights hills are moderate and you can skip the 
 climb up Reynolds Mountain.\nThere is no coffee stop along the route\, and
  no actual restrooms. We pass porto potties outside homes being renovated 
 or constructed.\nAlmost all of the route is on pavement. Wear appropriate 
 shoes and being snacks and water.\n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are
  no guest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release o
 f Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may hav
 e traffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Participants are responsible 
 for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a vo
 lunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is onl
 y to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you a
 cknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of in
 juries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and assoc
 iated with this event. You are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other 
 companions you bring with you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agre
 e to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.c
 om/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316918727
 /
